practiceProblems.problemStatement:
Fix the indentation and bracket structure of the following code so that if `tier = 1` and `points = 50`, it correctly outputs `Tier 1: Base Member`. Currently, due to missing braces, it outputs nothing.

Code to repair:
```java
int tier = 1, points = 50;
if (tier == 1)
    if (points >= 100)
        System.out.println("Tier 1: VIP Member");
else
    System.out.println("Tier 1: Base Member");
```

