practiceProblems.problemStatement:
In classic switch, declaring a variable in one case can cause a compilation collision. Fix the scope error by wrapping each case body in braces `{}`:
```java
int option = 1;
switch (option) {
    case 1: int result = 10; System.out.println("Res: " + result); break;
    case 2: int result = 20; System.out.println("Res: " + result); break;
}
```

